WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:07.140
Sudan is in the midst of what could be its
third civil war since independence.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:11.170
In a country traditionally dominated by the
military, fighting broke out in mid-April

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:13.920
to take control of Khartoum, the Sudanese
capital.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:17.420
The troops loyal to the general who presided
over the country were facing the militia led

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:20.779
by the man who up until then had been his
vice-president.

00:00:20.779 --> 00:00:22.740
Four months later, the struggle continues.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.800
Khartoum is being devastated and the violence
has spread to other parts of Sudan, taking

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.400
on the overtones of an ethnic conflict that
looks very bad.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.400
The country is descending into chaos.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.090
At the moment there are no reliable figures,
but everything indicates that the number of

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:40.800
fatalities in these four months amounts to
about 5,000 and that the fighting has caused

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.680
the displacement of more than 2 million people.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:47.910
And many of you will think: I’m not that
bothered about Sudan, I don't even know where

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:48.910
it is.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:53.730
Well, Sudan matters much more than you think.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:58.390
Similar in size to Mexico, Sudan is the third
largest country in Africa, and was the largest

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:01.030
of all before South Sudan's independence.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:05.540
It occupies a strategic location since its
coastline has access to the Red Sea, through

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:10.689
which routes that account for about 10% of
all world maritime trade pass.

00:01:10.689 --> 00:01:15.670
In addition, it has significant natural resources:
it has oil, it’s not exactly swimming in

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:18.470
dinosaur juice, but it does have modest crude
oil production.

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:21.170
And above all it has gold.

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:25.630
So much gold as to attract the attention of
Russia, or at least of the Wagner group, which

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:30.560
has links to one of the factions fighting
in Sudan while cashing in on its gold holdings.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.950
As if all this were not enough, in Sudan we
also have a clash between two traditionally

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:36.040
allied countries.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:39.810
We are talking about Saudi Arabia and the
United Arab Emirates, which are supporting

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.860
different sides.

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:48.740
What’s more, you should care about Sudan
because it could turn into an absolutely savage

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:49.740
war.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.600
You know that conflicts in Africa tend to
escalate into a bloodbath.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:57.070
UN Secretary General António Guterres has
already sounded the alarm bells.

00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:01.789
Entire neighborhoods have no running water
and limited electricity supplies, and more

00:02:01.789 --> 00:02:05.070
than two-thirds of hospitals near areas of
conflict cannot function.

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:10.140
I am particularly concerned by reports of
gender-based and sexual violence, and by the

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:12.890
ethnic dimension of the violence in Geneina.

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:17.780
Targeted attacks against civilians based on
their ethnic identities could amount to crimes

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:18.780
against humanity

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:23.980
So you see, even if it is purely out of humanitarian
interest, you have to know what is going on

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:24.980
in Sudan.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:28.269
So the question is: Why has such a brutal
conflict broken out in Sudan?

00:02:28.269 --> 00:02:31.180
What are the interests of the powers behind
both sides?

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:32.720
What could happen in the coming months?

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:40.100
Today on VisualPolitik we are going to answer
these questions, but first... let's look at

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:43.340
a bit of history.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:48.000
(DEVILS ON HORSEBACK)

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.440
In the early 19th century, the rulers of Ottoman
Egypt conquered what today corresponds to

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.060
most of the territory of Sudan.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:59.620
It was not until 1899 that Sudan became a
dominion of the British Empire.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:01.830
This colony gained its independence in 1956.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:04.599
And a lot of you will say: Well that’s great
news!

00:03:04.599 --> 00:03:08.269
How nice that the Sudanese could decide their
future by becoming a democracy!

00:03:08.269 --> 00:03:13.809
Well, it wasn’t to be the case.

00:03:13.809 --> 00:03:17.090
Sudan is the African country that has suffered
the most coups d'état.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:22.209
Since its independence, 16 coups have taken
place, six of which have been successful.

00:03:22.209 --> 00:03:26.489
In this way the military have put an end to
three attempts to establish democracy in the

00:03:26.489 --> 00:03:29.530
country, the most recent in 2021.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:35.500
Sudan has also experienced two civil wars,
one of 17 years and the other of 22 years.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:40.330
The conflict that broke out in April threatens
to be the third Sudanese civil war.

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:47.390
You heard correctly: out of the 67 years of
the Republic of Sudan, they have been fighting

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:50.120
for 39 years, more than half of them.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:54.310
It was South Sudan's struggle to create an
independent State with a majority Christian

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:57.020
population, while the rest of Sudan was essentially
Muslim.

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:00.430
Finally, the South Sudanese won their independence
in 2011.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:04.380
They took 25% of the territory and 75% of
its oil reserves.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.950
[That's right, with an agreement to share
this wealth].

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:10.620
However, these resources have been of little
use to the world's youngest country because,

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:16.579
surprise, surprise, in their 12 years of independence
they have already had their own 7-year civil

00:04:16.579 --> 00:04:17.579
war.

00:04:17.579 --> 00:04:21.130
But wait a minute, because the two civil wars
are only part of the Sudanese tragedy.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:23.050
Then there is also the Darfour conflict.

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:27.490
That's what the then UN Secretary General,
Kofi Annan, called it in 2006.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:32.849
(Annan Calls Darfur 'World's Worst Humanitarian
Crisis'.

00:04:32.849 --> 00:04:34.200
– RFERL)

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:39.789
In 1989, General Omar al-Bashir came to power
in Sudan.

00:04:39.789 --> 00:04:44.139
He ruled the country for 30 years and established
a dictatorship dominated from Khartoum by

00:04:44.139 --> 00:04:45.520
an Islamist elite.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:48.610
However, things were different in the peripheral
regions of the country.

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:53.009
In the Darfur region, black African ethnic
groups dedicated mainly to agriculture, such

00:04:53.009 --> 00:04:58.910
as the Fur, the Zaghawa and the Masalit, coexisted
with a population of Arab origin, dedicated

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:00.160
to pastoralism.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:03.450
Cattle breeders and farmers regularly fought
over territory.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:07.110
In 2003, the African ethnic groups, fed up
with the neglect to which they were subjected

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:10.130
by the central power in Khartoum, broke out
in rebellion.

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:11.550
Bashir sent in the army.

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:16.580
Then he turned to the Janjaweed.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:21.050
Janjaweed means demons on horseback and is
the name of the militia used by the Government

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:24.650
of Sudan as a counterinsurgency force against
ethnic Africans.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:29.460
Faced with little progress by the armed forces,
Bashir armed Arab nomadic cattle herders and

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:32.039
unleashed them on black African farmers.

00:05:32.039 --> 00:05:37.990
Ethnic cleansing was brutal, with 300,000
killed and up to 2.7 million people driven

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:42.889
from their homes.

00:05:42.889 --> 00:05:46.360
Sudan's military dictatorship already had
a track record that speaks for itself.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:51.100
It had been one of the four countries in the
world that supported Saddam Hussein when Iraq

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:52.100
invaded Kuwait.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:56.729
It had also hosted Osama bin Laden, who ran
al-Qaeda training camps in Sudan for a few

00:05:56.729 --> 00:05:58.690
years prior to 9/11.

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:02.950
So when the Government of Sudan commissioned
the Janjaweed to do the dirty work in Darfur,

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:08.539
Bashir became the target of all criticism
culminating in this situation in 2010.

00:06:08.539 --> 00:06:13.379
(International Criminal Court issues arrest
warrant for genocide against Bashir.

00:06:13.379 --> 00:06:14.379
– Reuters)

00:06:14.379 --> 00:06:17.940
Bashir became the first sitting Head of State
with a warrant for his arrest by the International

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:18.979
Criminal Court.

00:06:18.979 --> 00:06:22.759
It didn't do much good because Bashir continued
to rule Sudan as if nothing happened.

00:06:22.759 --> 00:06:26.950
And now I ask you: if you were the top ruler
of Sudan, what do you think would be the only

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:29.759
way to lose power besides dropping dead.

00:06:29.759 --> 00:06:32.880
Exactly, a coup d'état.

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:39.699
So to protect himself from his own armed forces,
Bashir officially regularized the Janjawed

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:43.830
by turning them into the Rapid Support Forces,
his own personal praetorian guard.

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:49.910
He placed his right-hand man in Darfur, Mohamed
Hamdan Dagalo, a warlord who calls himself

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:51.840
Hemedti, at the helm.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.319
But Bashir failed to see his ambition.

00:06:54.319 --> 00:06:58.460
(No one likes to eat crumbs from a feast;
everyone likes to sit at the table.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:06:59.460
– Sudanese proverb).

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:03.389
Internationally isolated, the Sudanese economy
was deteriorating and shortages were increasing.

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:08.150
Popular protests followed one after the other
and in April 2019 they achieved their goal.

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:10.220
Even so, to overthrow Bashir it would take...

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:12.910
Yes, you guessed it, a coup d'état.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:17.020
The armed forces gave Bashir the final push
when he saw that his dictatorship was at death's

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.410
door and Hemedti supported the coup.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:21.020
Bashir was expendable.

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:24.780
But losing their privileged position in Sudan
was something neither the armed forces nor

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:26.789
Hemedti were willing to allow.

00:07:26.789 --> 00:07:30.560
And as we say on VisualPolitik, no sooner
said than done.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:34.319
(Sudan's Top General Sworn In as Leader of
New Ruling Body.

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:35.319
– New York Times)

00:07:35.319 --> 00:07:39.250
General Burhan became the Head of State of
Sudan by presiding over the new Sovereign

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:40.250
Council.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:42.520
At his side he placed Hemedti as vice president.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:46.080
Because of course, you can't let loose the
guy who leads the Janjaweed, an armed force

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:47.560
of 100,000 soldiers.

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:51.169
Now, all this was not exactly a reason to
celebrate for the Sudanese.

00:07:51.169 --> 00:07:54.020
The people had not risen up against Bashir
to keep things the same.

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:58.159
So the military made a pact with the civilian
leadership: they would share power until elections

00:07:58.159 --> 00:08:00.199
were held in 2022.

00:08:00.199 --> 00:08:04.840
With these ingredients and Sudan's track record,
what could go wrong in the transition to democracy?

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:08.069
Yes, you guessed it: basically everything.

00:08:08.069 --> 00:08:12.690
Check it out.

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:15.800
(THE DEEP STATE VS.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:18.159
THE AFRICAN PRIGOZHIN)

00:08:18.159 --> 00:08:24.710
The 2019 power-sharing agreement between civilians
and the military was very fragile.

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:25.710
Why?

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:28.819
Well basically because there are countries
that may be much wealthier; but there are

00:08:28.819 --> 00:08:33.830
very few in which you can get richer from
power at the same level as in Sudan.

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:39.090
Former dictator Bashir had $130 million in
cash found in his home.

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:41.330
Yes, yes, in cash.

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:43.599
He controlled the Sudanese economy through
the military.

00:08:43.599 --> 00:08:46.850
And, of course, the other generals do not
have empty pockets either.

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:51.230
So when the new civilian government aspired
to set a level of transparency and accountability

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:56.160
worthy of the future democracy they intended
to bring to Sudan, General Burhan knew exactly

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:57.200
what he had to do.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:59.329
And no, he was not alone.

00:08:59.329 --> 00:09:03.350
(Sudan: Hemeti emerges from the shadows to
support Burhan's coup.

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:04.350
– MiddleEastEye)

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:07.360
Western donors and multilateral banks had
pledged billions of dollars to support the

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:08.709
democratic transition.

00:09:08.709 --> 00:09:14.020
But this coup by General Burhan and Hemedti
in October 2021 prevented much of that aid

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:18.579
from reaching Sudan.

00:09:18.579 --> 00:09:23.760
The United States, the World Bank and the
IMF stopped the flow of at least $1.4 billion

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:25.829
in aid and debt relief to Sudan.

00:09:25.829 --> 00:09:28.700
The military junta then had to cut wheat and
fuel subsidies.

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:32.470
The situation in Sudan became untenable and
the military was forced to negotiate with

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:35.490
civilians again to advance the democratic
transition.

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:37.720
Last December they reached an agreement.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:42.290
(Sudan to establish new civilian-led transitional
government on April 11.

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:43.290
– Africa News)

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:47.200
The problem with these agreements with the
military is that they have a lot to hide.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:51.350
General Burhan wants to protect what Sudanese
democrats call the "deep state".

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:55.510
We are talking about a whole network of corporations:
from banks and telecommunications companies,

00:09:55.510 --> 00:10:00.470
owned by Islamists and intelligence officers,
to companies owned by the armed forces itself

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:05.280
that dominate economic sectors such as arms
manufacturing, construction, agriculture and

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:06.300
transportation.

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:09.950
Something similar could be said of Hemedti,
who in recent years has become the African

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:12.350
Prigozhin.

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:16.600
Hemedti is much more than just a warlord.

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:20.790
Dictator Bashir let the Janjaweed take control
of the country's illicit gold mines, particularly

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:24.710
in the Darfur region, making Hemedti one of
the richest men in the country.

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:29.579
He has also gained even more money and allies
by using his Rapid Support Forces as mercenaries

00:10:29.579 --> 00:10:33.769
in the service of the United Arab Emirates
to fight in Yemen against the Houthi rebels

00:10:33.769 --> 00:10:40.589
and in Libya alongside General Khalifa Haftar.

00:10:40.589 --> 00:10:44.510
The new transitional agreement put Sudan's
two most powerful men on the ropes.

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:48.709
The terms were clear: Sudan would have one
single army under the command of the civilian

00:10:48.709 --> 00:10:52.829
government and the Rapid Support Forces would
have to be integrated into it.

00:10:52.829 --> 00:10:55.459
This clearly threatened the privileged position
of both.

00:10:55.459 --> 00:11:00.089
That of General Burhan, since the agreement
set democratic elections for 2024.

00:11:00.089 --> 00:11:04.470
And also that of Hemedti, since within two
years he had to integrate his militia into

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:08.860
the Army, something that the African Prigozhin
intended to delay for a decade.

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:13.420
Therefore, the only way out for both was armed
combat to see which of the two would prevail

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:15.389
in deciding the future of Sudan.

00:11:15.389 --> 00:11:18.850
And so the country's capital is taking the
brunt of it.

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:22.560
(Streets of Khartoum are devastated by military
conflict.

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:23.560
– Sky)

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:25.660
The problem with this conflict is that it
is a balanced fight.

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:27.529
It will be difficult for either side to prevail.

00:11:27.529 --> 00:11:34.170
The Sudanese armed forces is not worth much,
but it has aviation.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:37.850
The Rapid Support Forces are better armed
and more skilled in combat thanks to their

00:11:37.850 --> 00:11:39.430
experience as mercenaries.

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:43.800
Their soldiers have had no qualms about taking
over homes, schools and even hospitals to

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:47.769
fortify themselves in Khartoum and to take
the fight one street at a time.

00:11:47.769 --> 00:11:50.620
Now, the armed forces have intensively bombarded
the capital.

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:54.440
And as if this were not enough, the fighting
has spread to the rest of Sudan, resurrecting

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:58.529
old ghosts from the past that threaten to
lead to another ethnic conflict.

00:11:58.529 --> 00:12:00.000
Check it out.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:05.389
(Darfur: Aid workers witness hundreds of murdered
bodies including children abandoned in streets.

00:12:05.389 --> 00:12:06.389
– Reliefweb)

00:12:06.389 --> 00:12:10.410
The Janjaweed ride again and the risk of further
genocide gains momentum as the conflict drags

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:11.410
on.

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:14.620
Hemedti stands as the rebel force that has
risen up against the legitimate government

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:15.620
of Sudan.

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:19.670
But the latter is also questionable given
the coup record of General Burhan, who is

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:22.370
not exactly the best friend of Sudanese democrats.

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:25.700
The support of foreign powers could tip the
balance one way or the other, and there are

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:27.079
many interests at stake.

00:12:27.079 --> 00:12:28.230
What interests are we talking about?

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:35.790
We are going to take a look at that right
now.

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:43.100
(THE TREASURE OF THE RED SEA)

00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:46.339
The main powers in the Red Sea are Saudi Arabia
and Egypt.

00:12:46.339 --> 00:12:49.550
It is therefore in their interest to maintain
the status quo in the area.

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:51.420
That means in Sudan as well.

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:56.410
Especially after the fall of the Bashir dictatorship,
which had moved very close to its rivals Turkey

00:12:56.410 --> 00:12:57.410
and Qatar.

00:12:57.410 --> 00:13:01.520
Saudi Arabia and Egypt were comfortable with
the military junta of Burhan and Hemedti.

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:05.490
Their main objective in Sudan was to prevent
a democratic revolution in the Arab world.

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:08.160
That is why they supported post-Bashir Sudan.

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:10.730
Saudi Arabia pledged to invest $3 billion.

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:14.130
But wait a minute, because the United Arab
Emirates doubled the bet.

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:15.209
Why so much interest?

00:13:15.209 --> 00:13:17.310
The Red Sea holds the answer:

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:22.410
(UAE to build port in Sudan as part of $6bn
investment package . – AGBI)

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:26.779
Despite being traditional allies, as you can
imagine, this Emirate port is of no interest

00:13:26.779 --> 00:13:28.800
to either Saudi Arabia or Egypt.

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:33.779
What’s more, Riyadh's favorite is General
Burhan, who is also General Al-Sisi's favorite

00:13:33.779 --> 00:13:36.980
because of the close ties between the Sudanese
and Egyptian armies.

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:42.420
However, VisualPolitik community, I have already
told you that the UAE's man in Sudan is Hemedti.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:46.970
So all these crossed interests tie in with
Abu Dhabi's growing strategy to deploy its

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:54.910
full economic potential to rival Saudi Arabia
as the Arab world's benchmark.

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:59.150
While Prince Bin Salman fell out of favor
in the West after Khashoggi's murder, the

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:03.260
United Arab Emirates has tried to portray
itself as the friendly face of the region.

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:07.131
In the end they have shown different interests
in Yemen and in Washington, where Abu Dhabi

00:14:07.131 --> 00:14:15.019
has tried to replace Riyadh as America's favorite
military ally in the Gulf.

00:14:15.019 --> 00:14:19.170
Bin Salman has not shied away from the rivalry
and is now trying to make up lost ground.

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:21.420
We can see it at the sporting level.

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:24.990
The Emirates buy Manchester City, so the Saudis
buy Newcastle.

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:28.720
There's Formula 1 in Abu Dhabi, so there's
Formula 1 in Saudi Arabia.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:29.750
And so on.

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:34.009
Therefore, returning to the war in Sudan,
right now the priority of the regional powers

00:14:34.009 --> 00:14:38.050
is not so much peace, but rather that the
side they support prevails.

00:14:38.050 --> 00:14:40.589
Even more so if we add the Wagner Group into
the equation.

00:14:40.589 --> 00:14:44.370
The gold that Hemedti gets in Sudan is being
smuggled to Russia through the Emirates.

00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:49.200
It has taken the White House a while, but
it finally made a move against Abu Dhabi.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.200
Look:

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:54.800
(Two arms companies linked to the Sudanese
army, have been sanctioned by the US.

00:14:54.800 --> 00:15:00.550
Meanwhile, Al Junaid, a gold trading operation
controlled by Hemeti and his brother, and

00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:04.110
UAE-based Tradive, have also been sanctioned
– Middle East Eye)

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:07.130
The Wagner group's links to Hemedti date back
to 2017.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:13.959
In principle, Wagner would have given weapons
and military training to the Rapid Support

00:15:13.959 --> 00:15:16.089
Forces in exchange for access to Sudan's gold.

00:15:16.089 --> 00:15:17.089
If we had made this video months ago, we would
now be telling you about how Russia is spreading

00:15:17.089 --> 00:15:18.089
its influence across Africa.

00:15:18.089 --> 00:15:19.089
But after the Prigozhin mutiny the scenario
has changed.

00:15:19.089 --> 00:15:20.089
Or maybe not so much.

00:15:20.089 --> 00:15:21.089
If the Kremlin wants to maintain the alliances
achieved by Wagner, as staged at the summit

00:15:21.089 --> 00:15:22.089
with African countries recently held in St.
Petersburg, it needs Prigozhin.

00:15:22.089 --> 00:15:23.089
And his finances even more.

00:15:23.089 --> 00:15:24.089
(Russia's economy is being propped up by Wagner
Group's gold-smuggling operations, UK government

00:15:24.089 --> 00:15:25.089
report says.

00:15:25.089 --> 00:15:26.089
– BusinessInsider)

00:15:26.089 --> 00:15:27.089
Sudan's gold is too attractive for the Kremlin
and Wagner to drop Hemedti.

00:15:27.089 --> 00:15:31.780
Burhan also has good support with Saudi Arabia,
which in 2022 was the world's fifth largest

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:35.850
military spender, behind only the United States,
China, Russia and India.

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:39.139
So all indications are that the war in Sudan
is going to drag on.

00:15:39.139 --> 00:15:43.769
We will be watching closely as these conflicts
tend to unleash enormous amounts of violence.

00:15:43.769 --> 00:15:48.389
In the meantime, the question is over to you:
How do you think the situation in Sudan will

00:15:48.389 --> 00:15:49.389
evolve?

00:15:49.389 --> 00:15:51.459
Will any of the foreign powers be directly
involved?

00:15:51.459 --> 00:15:53.410
You can leave me your answer in the comments.

